WHAT IS UNDER A DIFFERENT LICENSE

Forge (https://github.com/Card-Forge/forge) is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3. Two kinds of Forge-derived material are in this
tree, and both remain under that license (full text in LICENSE-GPL-3.0):

  * The Java bridge under packages/forge-export/bridge/, whose files carry
    `SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only`. It is compiled against an
    installed Forge and runs as a separate process.

  * Lines of Forge card script quoted as evidence of what a Forge release
    does: the play-admission records under packages/data/data/ (chiefly each
    `script-coverage.json`), packages/data/data/forge-syntax-review-v1.json,
    packages/data/data/legacy-cube-2021-forge-decisions-v1.json, and the
    exact-script checks in packages/data/src/legacy-cube/ and its tests.

Section 13 of the GNU GPL version 3 permits combining a work under it with a
work under the GNU Affero GPL version 3. Each part keeps its own license, and
the AGPL's network-interaction requirement applies to the combination.

Forge itself is not in this tree. It is downloaded separately (see
tools/forge/README.md) and is never redistributed here.


WHAT NO LICENSE HERE COVERS

The licenses above are granted over the source code, tests, documentation and
generated example content in this repository. They are not, and cannot be, a
grant of rights in material this project does not own:

  * Magic: The Gathering, its rules text, card names, mana symbols, set names
    and other marks are the property of Wizards of the Coast LLC. Nothing here
    licenses any of it.

  * The printed-set catalogs under packages/data/data/ carry card names, types
    and rules text taken from Scryfall (https://scryfall.com) under its API
    guidelines. Card images and symbol artwork are not redistributed; they are
    fetched on demand and cached locally.

  * The mana symbols this project draws are original shapes on the categories
    each color has always used. The SVG path data is the authors' work and is
    covered by the license above. The symbol designs themselves are Wizards'
    and are not.

  * Using this software together with Wizards' intellectual property is subject
    to the Wizards Fan Content Policy, which permits such use only on a
    non-commercial basis. That policy governs that use; it is not a restriction
    added to the license above, and the license does not override it.

This project is unofficial Fan Content. It is not approved, endorsed,
sponsored or affiliated with Wizards of the Coast in any way.
